Subject: dhl.com IN ANY

I meant to write about this a while ago but decided
to return as I'm currently lamenting how clueless
I am, egh... so much data, so little insight!

(I should be paying more attention in my R class,
oh well.  Tidyverse sounds like something that would
be very appropriate for this occasion.)

Just now I re-ran the command (that I shamefully have
the only copy of in Claude) on March 19
(2026-03-19T22:16:33.907407Z to be specific)
that produces a histogram of dhl.com IN ANY requests
made per hour, scaled down by a factor of 5000:

# perl -ne 'next unless /dhl.com IN ANY/; if (my ($D,$H) = /(\d{,2})-Mar-2026 (\d{,2})/) { $Bin{"Mar-$D $H:00"}++ } else { die }; END { foreach (sort { $a cmp $b } keys %Bin) { printf "%s %s\n", $_, "=" x int($Bin{$_} / 5000.0) } }' /var/log/bind/queries*
