The last time I checked it appeared as a persistent attack
of 41 x 5000 requests per hour.  Now there's a spike with
at least 66 x 5000 requests at March 24, 19:00 UTC.  That's
like... 330000 with 4 zeros!  In an hour!

But here's the really weird thing about it: it's not just
one or two naughty IPs doing it.  Granted a handful of them
take the naughty leaderboard (but that hasn't changed since
March 19.  Indicative that the second spike is different...)

